  "ui2e2fa0ad4e93": "Import forms, project packages and study maps before leaving connectivity. Prepare offline basemaps where supported; online map tiles need internet. Save field records locally and sync the selected project when connected. Sync sends responses, GIS/study features and photos. Records sync in sequential batches of at most 20. Busy-server responses retry automatically; completed batches remain synced after interruption. Retry sends only remaining records. The supplied backend updates stable record IDs and reuses photo IDs. Saved edits increment response_revision and return to the upload queue. The revisions tab preserves uploaded versions; several offline edits before sync upload only the final version. Deploy the new Code.gs to sync corrections. A conflict stays on the phone for manager review.\n\nManagers: reload the Google spreadsheet → MapBanai → Map workspace or Charts workspace. Maps use the app’s basemaps, designs, independent fonts, category colours and symbols, editable legends and PNG/JPEG downloads. Manager maps accept multiple GeoJSON or shapefile ZIP overlays. Both map and chart workspaces have Fullscreen, with an expanded Sheets dialog when browser fullscreen is blocked. Charts include aggregation, themes and PNG/JPEG/SVG export. These workspaces require an authenticated manager and are not public links.\n\nCollected records are stored as full JSON (including geometry and answers) across json_1 to json_4 output columns. Concatenate those columns to reconstruct a record. The photos tab includes readable metadata, embedded thumbnails and Open photo in Drive links. New uploads add previews automatically. For previously synced photos, reload the spreadsheet and choose MapBanai → Refresh photo previews (up to 50 missing previews per run). Files remain private; the spreadsheet shows embedded thumbnails to its viewers. If a preview cannot be created, use its Drive link. This backend is an upload destination; it does not automatically download other enumerators’ records into your phone.",
  "@ui2e2fa0ad4e93": {
    "description": "Import forms, project packages and study maps before leaving connectivity. Prepare offline basemaps where supported; online map tiles need internet. Save field records locally and sync the selected project when connected. Sync sends responses, GIS/study features and photos. Records sync in sequential batches of at most 20. Busy-server responses retry automatically; completed batches remain synced after interruption. Retry sends only remaining records. The supplied backend updates stable record IDs and reuses photo IDs. Saved edits increment response_revision and return to the upload queue. The revisions tab preserves uploaded versions; several offline edits before sync upload only the final version. Deploy the new Code.gs to sync corrections. A conflict stays on the phone for manager review.\n\nManagers: reload the Google spreadsheet → MapBanai → Map workspace or Charts workspace. Maps use the app’s basemaps, designs, independent fonts, category colours and symbols, editable legends and PNG/JPEG downloads. Manager maps accept multiple GeoJSON or shapefile ZIP overlays. Both map and chart workspaces have Fullscreen, with an expanded Sheets dialog when browser fullscreen is blocked. Charts include aggregation, themes and PNG/JPEG/SVG export. These workspaces require an authenticated manager and are not public links.\n\nCollected records are stored as full JSON (including geometry and answers) across json_1 to json_4 output columns. Concatenate those columns to reconstruct a record. The photos tab includes readable metadata, embedded thumbnails and Open photo in Drive links. New uploads add previews automatically. For previously synced photos, reload the spreadsheet and choose MapBanai → Refresh photo previews (up to 50 missing previews per run). Files remain private; the spreadsheet shows embedded thumbnails to its viewers. If a preview cannot be created, use its Drive link. This backend is an upload destination; it does not automatically download other enumerators’ records into your phone."
  },
