  "uia71aaef663f0": "Open Project Details → Reusable templates. Save the whole project or its selected layer and questionnaire. From Project Setup → Reusable templates, create a new project from a saved template. Project Details also lets you add template layers to the current project. Templates preserve forms, layer names and setup; they exclude site geometry, visits, photos and cloud keys. New projects and added layers receive fresh identities. Configure the new project’s cloud connection separately. Templates are local and included in database backups. To share with another phone, create a project from the template and export its project package.",
  "@uia71aaef663f0": {
    "description": "Open Project Details → Reusable templates. Save the whole project or its selected layer and questionnaire. From Project Setup → Reusable templates, create a new project from a saved template. Project Details also lets you add template layers to the current project. Templates preserve forms, layer names and setup; they exclude site geometry, visits, photos and cloud keys. New projects and added layers receive fresh identities. Configure the new project’s cloud connection separately. Templates are local and included in database backups. To share with another phone, create a project from the template and export its project package."
  },
  "ui78f2a306509a": "Open WebMap for the selected project. Use Explore → Colours & categories: choose any text/numeric answer column (such as layer), then Categories for per-value colours and visibility or Graduated for numeric colours. Geometry type is the uniform default. Edit category names, colours and symbols in Download Map. Filter and inspect features, choose a map theme, turn labels on/off, and compose a poster or map-only image with a title and subtitle. Export PNG for clear graphics or JPEG for smaller files. Tap the separate Download Map button to open 12 designs, custom colours, portrait/landscape, aspect ratio and pixel resolution (HD, Full HD, QHD, 4K or custom). Download PNG/JPEG opens the phone file picker; Share PNG/JPEG opens sharing. Basemap tiles must be loaded and exportable; offline/data-only exports may lack the basemap. Rename mapped legend categories, choose point symbols/line patterns/polygon outlines or upload PNG/self-contained SVG icons (up to 512 KB and 2048 pixels per side). Title, subtitle and legend fonts can be chosen independently, with four bundled offline fonts. Text, symbols and north arrow scale with image resolution; choose Standard/Large/Extra large for readability. The map covers over 80% of the exported poster, with a compact title and legend below. Map extent defaults to Fit visible data; choose Current map view to preserve your framing. Coordinates below the title are omitted. Only included basemaps receive attribution; record counts and no-basemap notices are omitted.",
  "@ui78f2a306509a": {
    "description": "Open WebMap for the selected project. Use Explore → Colours & categories: choose any text/numeric answer column (such as layer), then Categories for per-value colours and visibility or Graduated for numeric colours. Geometry type is the uniform default. Edit category names, colours and symbols in Download Map. Filter and inspect features, choose a map theme, turn labels on/off, and compose a poster or map-only image with a title and subtitle. Export PNG for clear graphics or JPEG for smaller files. Tap the separate Download Map button to open 12 designs, custom colours, portrait/landscape, aspect ratio and pixel resolution (HD, Full HD, QHD, 4K or custom). Download PNG/JPEG opens the phone file picker; Share PNG/JPEG opens sharing. Basemap tiles must be loaded and exportable; offline/data-only exports may lack the basemap. Rename mapped legend categories, choose point symbols/line patterns/polygon outlines or upload PNG/self-contained SVG icons (up to 512 KB and 2048 pixels per side). Title, subtitle and legend fonts can be chosen independently, with four bundled offline fonts. Text, symbols and north arrow scale with image resolution; choose Standard/Large/Extra large for readability. The map covers over 80% of the exported poster, with a compact title and legend below. Map extent defaults to Fit visible data; choose Current map view to preserve your framing. Coordinates below the title are omitted. Only included basemaps receive attribution; record counts and no-basemap notices are omitted."
  },
  "ui0f3c63f41614": "Open a study-area feature → Site timeline / add observation, or select a feature in the guided visit screen → Site timeline. Choose Add observation / start visit to record another measurement. Finish each visit separately; earlier answers remain linked to the same stable feature UUID. Choose a questionnaire and numeric question (such as salinity) to compare visits. Keep question names and units consistent. Export all observations as CSV; feature_uuid joins them to study-map GeoJSON. Imported visit history is included and deduplicated with local interviews. Timelines show locally available history; cloud sync does not download other devices’ visits.",
  "@ui0f3c63f41614": {
    "description": "Open a study-area feature → Site timeline / add observation, or select a feature in the guided visit screen → Site timeline. Choose Add observation / start visit to record another measurement. Finish each visit separately; earlier answers remain linked to the same stable feature UUID. Choose a questionnaire and numeric question (such as salinity) to compare visits. Keep question names and units consistent. Export all observations as CSV; feature_uuid joins them to study-map GeoJSON. Imported visit history is included and deduplicated with local interviews. Timelines show locally available history; cloud sync does not download other devices’ visits."
  },
  "ui4452be7b875c": "Project packages share project definitions, forms and study-layer configuration; they are not a backup of responses or photos. “Include sync connection” is optional and includes the URL and key. Preserve the same project identity across the team; duplicating a project creates a different identity that needs its own backend configuration.\n\nUse the app backup/export tools for collected data and keep copies outside the phone. Installing an update over the existing signed app preserves local storage; uninstalling or clearing app storage removes local information. Save cloud connection settings before exporting a package.",
  "@ui4452be7b875c": {
    "description": "Project packages share project definitions, forms and study-layer configuration; they are not a backup of responses or photos. “Include sync connection” is optional and includes the URL and key. Preserve the same project identity across the team; duplicating a project creates a different identity that needs its own backend configuration.\n\nUse the app backup/export tools for collected data and keep copies outside the phone. Installing an update over the existing signed app preserves local storage; uninstalling or clearing app storage removes local information. Save cloud connection settings before exporting a package."
  },
  "ui48f8d1dd5266": "Recommended: one Google workbook + one Apps Script web app + one private API key per project. Keep questionnaire tabs (survey, choices, settings) and output tabs (responses, features, photos, revisions) in the same workbook. No second URL or key is needed.\n\nFor separate storage, use two workbooks: questionnaireSheetId points to the XLSForm workbook; dataSheetId points to the collected-data workbook. The same script handles both, so the app still uses one URL and key. Two independent deployments/keys are not configured in this version.\n\nUse a separate setup for each project. Keep questionnaire editing with managers; enumerators only need the MapBanai project package. API keys give access to the project endpoint; share packages containing them only with your field team.",
  "@ui48f8d1dd5266": {
    "description": "Recommended: one Google workbook + one Apps Script web app + one private API key per project. Keep questionnaire tabs (survey, choices, settings) and output tabs (responses, features, photos, revisions) in the same workbook. No second URL or key is needed.\n\nFor separate storage, use two workbooks: questionnaireSheetId points to the XLSForm workbook; dataSheetId points to the collected-data workbook. The same script handles both, so the app still uses one URL and key. Two independent deployments/keys are not configured in this version.\n\nUse a separate setup for each project. Keep questionnaire editing with managers; enumerators only need the MapBanai project package. API keys give access to the project endpoint; share packages containing them only with your field team."
  },
