  "uice44f8239f96": "Open Study Area from Home and select Field Verification, Recurring Collection or Study Area Visits. Choose the project, site layer and questionnaire. Assign each uploaded layer to its workflows in Project layers. Field Verification updates baseline features; tap a site and its questionnaire button to start or resume a guided visit. Recurring Collection uses a Collection round with a name, optional period/season and date. Each round keeps independent collected, not collected and needs review states. To build recurring sites from first measurements, choose Create layer from responses, then the source questionnaire and numeric measurement. Original responses remain intact. Study Area Visits supports quick done, undone and review states with optional questionnaires. Open Google Maps from the selected site for external navigation. Timelines preserve previous observations. Uploaded site names and attributes remain as supplied; choose a bilingual XLSForm to translate questionnaire labels.",
  "@uice44f8239f96": {
    "description": "Open Study Area from Home and select Field Verification, Recurring Collection or Study Area Visits. Choose the project, site layer and questionnaire. Assign each uploaded layer to its workflows in Project layers. Field Verification updates baseline features; tap a site and its questionnaire button to start or resume a guided visit. Recurring Collection uses a Collection round with a name, optional period/season and date. Each round keeps independent collected, not collected and needs review states. To build recurring sites from first measurements, choose Create layer from responses, then the source questionnaire and numeric measurement. Original responses remain intact. Study Area Visits supports quick done, undone and review states with optional questionnaires. Open Google Maps from the selected site for external navigation. Timelines preserve previous observations. Uploaded site names and attributes remain as supplied; choose a bilingual XLSForm to translate questionnaire labels."
  },
